{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791310835,"nonce":"VuqnA5tyCvA55/Fhuq1G3QJ4tKQ=","title":"Inherited generic fields bind parent parameters by the child's parameter names","message":"Reproducer: /tmp/rayzor-inherited-type-arguments-probe/InheritedTypeArguments.hx. ArgumentChild\u003cT\u003e extends ArgumentParent\u003cArray\u003cT\u003e\u003e, whose value field has the parent's T type. Reading new ArgumentChild\u003cInt\u003e([7]).value must produce Array\u003cInt\u003e. Native Haxe prints CONFORMANCE_OK; rayzor at 4ea314bb564aadebf8baf1c1561a676a06bf283f plus the virtual-accessor prototype throws \"inherited array field type\" because Std.isOfType(value, Array) is false.\n\nAstLowering::substitute_receiver_type builds bindings only from the receiver's own parameters, then matches any remaining parameter by its bare name. It consequently binds the parent's T directly to the child's Int instead of following extends ArgumentParent\u003cArray\u003cT\u003e\u003e. The superclass instantiation needs to participate in substitution before same-name fallback. The failure also applies to inherited properties with an overridden getter returning Array\u003cT\u003e.\n\nIssue11010 advances from an uncompiled-main crash to a wrong answer with virtual property dispatch and constructor initializer ordering repaired. Its property result is an array pointer but the call site boxes it with haxe_box_int_ptr; the expected parent type argument is Array\u003cT\u003e. This is distinct from the accessor dispatch and initialization issues.","files":null}]}